# Windows files should use crlf line endings
# https://help.github.com/articles/dealing-with-line-endings/
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Machine-written translation memory shards (i18n_generate_translations.yml,
# one file per locale). A line-wise auto-merge of two divergent shards can
# produce duplicated keys or invalid JSON that the next pipeline run trusts —
# force any divergence to a loud conflict instead. Deliberately NOT
# linguist-generated: the batch PR review is the memory's only content gate,
# so the diff must stay visible; per-locale sharding keeps it small.
.i18n/memory/*.json merge=binary

# Casebook coverage matrices are regenerated by the engine (bun casebook:generate); review the cases, not the table.
packages/casebook/*/COVERAGE_MATRIX.md linguist-generated
